{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+, Antifungal, candidacidal, Antibiofilm", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that the sequence of this peptide shows 94.73% similarity to Phylloseptin-1.1TR. It only differs from AP2989 at position 4 (M for this peptide and L for AP2989: Phylloseptin-1.1TR). Activity: Active against S. aureus (MIC 8 ug/ml), E.coli (MIC 128 ug/ml)), C. albicans (MIC 16 ug/ml)). Updated 7/2021", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "27589802", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Toxins (Basel). 2016 Aug 31;8(9). pii: E255. doi: 10.3390/toxins8090255. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP02867", "source_id": "AP02867", "source_numeric_id": "02867", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP02867", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Discovery of Novel Bacterial Cell-Penetrating Phylloseptins in Defensive Skin Secretions of the South American Hylid Frogs, Phyllomedusa duellmani and Phyllomedusa coelestis.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal, candidacidal", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Activity: Active against E. coli (MIC 100 uM), S. epidermidis (MIC 12.5 uM), and C. albicans (MIC 25 uM). SAR: This amidated form is more active than the non-amidated form. Variant: Phylloseptin-3.3TR ( Mechkarska et al., 2018) share the same sequence but C-terminally amidated. Active against C. albicans (MIC 100 uM). Discovery: Found in multiple species, including that by Conlon2018. Updated 2/2018; 7/2021; merged with AP2994 (amidated) 2/2023.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "27589802", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Toxins (Basel). 2016 Aug 31;8(9). pii: E255. doi: 10.3390/toxins8090255. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP02992", "source_id": "AP02992", "source_numeric_id": "02992", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP02992", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Discovery of Novel Bacterial Cell-Penetrating Phylloseptins in Defensive Skin Secretions of the South American Hylid Frogs, Phyllomedusa duellmani and Phyllomedusa", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
